    <td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="postbody">Thanks for the link. It was an interesting read, but the poster sounds like a raving fanboi. So much of the stuff he was raving about I was thinking "Gee, EQ had that 4 years ago." <img src="images/smiles/icon_wink.gif" alt="Wink" border="0" /> Things like "The world is huge.. hour and 45 minutes to get from one side to the other." Even pre-expansion EQ could boast something similar. Other stuff was just typical MMORPG stuff that *every* game has, so i'm not sure why this guy was so excited since he mentioned that he has played DAoC and EQ.
<br />

<br />
Alot of it sounds like normal dev tripe as well, the typical spin to get the fanboi's worked into a hypnotic frenzy. Some of the comments involving the developers standpoint on some issues seemed especially naive.
<br />

<br />
However, there were some nice little tidbits buried in there every once in a while. I like the variety and differences they are putting in for the different factions, like different mounts. 
<br />

<br />
Still looking forward to the game, but i'm too jaded to buy all the hype. <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="Smile" border="0" /></span><span class="gensmall"><i></i></span></td>
